EXPERIMENT 11 – SELENIUM WEBDRIVER: VERIFY PAGE TITLE AND URL

AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to open the Chrome browser and verify the title and URL of a web page.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the Selenium 4 dependency.
2. Create the ChromeDriver object and maximize the browser.
3. Open the web page using driver.get().
4. Read the page title using getTitle() and URL using getCurrentUrl().
5. Compare the title with the expected title "Swag Labs" and display PASS or FAIL.
6. Close the browser using driver.quit().
CODE
Exercise11.java
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;

public class Exercise11 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();
            driver.get("https://www.saucedemo.com");

            String title = driver.getTitle();
            String url = driver.getCurrentUrl();

            System.out.println("Page title : " + title);
            System.out.println("Current URL : " + url);

            if (title.equals("Swag Labs") &&
                url.contains("saucedemo")) {
                System.out.println("Title verification : PASS");
            } else {
                System.out.println("Title verification : FAIL");
            }
        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
- Website URL: https://www.saucedemo.com
- Expected title: Swag Labs
OUTPUT
Page title : Swag Labs
Current URL : https://www.saucedemo.com/
Title verification : PASS


RESULT
Thus, the Selenium WebDriver program to open Chrome and verify the title and URL of a web page was executed successfully.
